# Build context for deploy/walking-skeleton/Dockerfile.server.
#
# The context is the REPO ROOT (RC F4: the server references five sibling src/ projects and bakes
# in the canonical card data), but the image COPYs exactly four paths. Without this file fly
# uploads the whole working tree on every deploy — measured 2026-08-15 at 16 GB / 86,570 files,
# of which unity/ was 15 GB, .git/ 843 MB and art-pipeline/ 568 MB. The first three paths totalled
# ~2.9 MB then; the bot model (2026-10-18) adds 3.3 MB.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST: deny everything, then re-admit only what the Dockerfile reads. Each parent
# directory has to be re-admitted and then re-emptied (`!unity/` then `unity/*`) or the exception
# for the nested path can never be reached. Written this way rather than as a denylist so that a
# new top-level directory is excluded by default instead of silently re-inflating the upload.
#
# RETIREMENT TRIGGER: adding a COPY to Dockerfile.server means adding its path here, in the same
# commit — a missing entry fails the build with "file not found", which reads like a bad COPY path
# rather than an ignore rule.

*

# --- src/ : the server plus its eight transitive project references, and Directory.Build.props ---
!src/

# Windows-restored intermediates must NOT enter a Linux build: obj/project.assets.json pins
# absolute package paths under C:\Users\...\.nuget\packages, which do not exist in the container.
src/**/bin/
src/**/obj/

# --- card definitions: source of truth is the Unity tree (Dockerfile.server line 15) ---
!unity/
unity/*
!unity/Assets/
unity/Assets/*
!unity/Assets/CardData/

# --- AI-opponent bot roster (Dockerfile.server line 18) ---
!tooling/
tooling/*
!tooling/data/
tooling/data/*
!tooling/data/bot-roster.json
# --- the bot's network (Dockerfile.server, COPY tooling/data/bot-model/) ---
!tooling/data/bot-model/

# The web card authoring tool (deploy/cardweb/Dockerfile). This file is an ALLOWLIST -- it opens
# with `*`, so anything not re-included here is simply absent from the build context and the
# COPY silently produces an empty directory rather than an error.
!tooling/cardweb/
# ...but never someone's staged edits or editor comments. Both are in-flight author work, not
# corpus, and baking either into an image would resurrect it on every deploy. In production both
# live on the volume (EMBERFALL_STAGING_DIR / EMBERFALL_COMMENTS_DIR), so the image needs neither.
tooling/cardweb/staging/
tooling/cardweb/comments/
# The corpus analytics panel, served as the "Corpus" tab (deploy/cardweb/Dockerfile).
!tooling/card-admin/
# ...minus its generated data, which is 260 KB of a rollup the server recomputes per request off
# the corpus it actually loaded. Shipping it would only make a stale copy reachable.
tooling/card-admin/data.js
tooling/card-admin/data.json
# ...and never a locally-built bytecode cache. `*` denies everything, so a `!dir/` re-admits the
# whole directory including one somebody's local run left behind.
tooling/cardweb/__pycache__/
tooling/card-admin/__pycache__/
# corpus.py imports art_file() from this module instead of re-deriving the art filename.
!tooling/scripts/
tooling/scripts/*
!tooling/scripts/gen_card_prompt_briefs.py
